'pragmat'title="where failure goes".
$ Predict which calls reach the second alternative of choose.

'q'choose+>n+value>:
   n>0,n<10,10->value;
   20->value.

$ A failed guard tries the next alternative. A later failure exits choose.
'a'test+>n-value:
   choose+n+value,printf+"%d gives %d%n"+n+value;
   printf+"%d fails%n"+n.

'root'test+-1,test+4,test+12.
'end'
